## 7. Key terms (mini glossary)

| Term | Plain meaning |
|---|---|
| **Late-delivery risk** | The label we predict: 1 = the order was delivered late, 0 = on time. |
| **Pre-dispatch** | Known before the parcel leaves the warehouse (so usable for early warning). |
| **Risk score** | The model's estimated probability (0–100%) that the order is late. |
| **Raw score vs. calibrated score** | Raw = the model's direct output (used for *ranking* quality). Calibrated = adjusted so that "70%" really means ~70% of such orders are late (used for *decisions*, tiers and probabilities). |
| **Risk tier** | Low / Medium / High band of the calibrated score. |
| **Flagged** | An order in the **High** tier. |
| **Precision** | Of the orders we flag, the share that really are late. |
| **Recall (coverage)** | Of all late orders, the share we manage to flag. |
| **False alarm / missed order** | A flagged order that was on time / a late order that was not flagged. |
| **ROC-AUC** | Chance that a randomly chosen late order gets a higher score than a randomly chosen on-time one. 0.5 = guessing, 1.0 = perfect. |
| **PR-AUC** | Area under the precision-recall curve; compare it with the late rate (what a guesser scores). |
| **Confidence interval (CI)** | The range within which the true value plausibly lies (here from 1,000 bootstrap resamples). |
| **Calibration / ECE** | How honest the probabilities are. Expected Calibration Error: lower is better. |
| **Lift** | How many times more late orders a group contains than average. |
| **SHAP** | A method that splits one prediction into the contribution of each feature. |
| **Leakage** | Accidentally letting the model see information from the future (or the answer itself). Strictly forbidden here. |
| **Chronological split** | Train on the past, validate on the next period, test on the newest period. |
| **Proxy target** | A stand-in for what we really care about. Late delivery stands in for "delivery trouble", not for RTO. |
| **PSI** | Population Stability Index: how much a feature's distribution has drifted. |

