## 16. Rebuild everything from scratch

Only needed if you want to regenerate the data, models and documents yourself.

1. Complete the Quick start (steps 1–3).
2. Download `DataCoSupplyChainDataset.csv` ([DOI](https://doi.org/10.17632/8gx2fvg2k6.5)) into `data/raw/`.
3. Run the whole pipeline:

```bash
python run_all.py
```

It takes roughly **30–60 minutes** (SHAP and multi-seed tuning dominate), stops on the first failing script, and writes `outputs/run_log.txt`. The run is deterministic: running it twice yields the same final model.

Or run individual steps (in this order):

```bash
python src/01_prepare.py              # wrangle & feature-engineer
python src/02_train.py                # train 5 models, compare
python src/05_tune_multiseed.py       # tune final LightGBM + calibrate + stability
python src/03_calibrate_threshold.py  # cluster-aware tiers + thresholds
python src/04_explain.py              # SHAP plots
python src/06_robustness.py           # ablations, backtest, PSI
python src/07_predict_demo.py         # demo orders
python src/08_sanity_checks.py        # sanity checks
python src/09_verification.py         # label-artifact / confound studies
python src/10_finalize.py             # -> outputs/final_metrics.json
python src/11_experiments.py          # extra experiments (read-only)
python src/11_render_docs.py          # regenerate README, MODEL_CARD, report_tables
```

> The Random Forest model file is ~566 MB and is not committed; it is regenerated in step 2.

**Editing documentation:** do not edit `README.md`, `MODEL_CARD.md` or `docs/VIVA_CHEATSHEET.md` directly. Edit the files in `templates/` and run `python src/11_render_docs.py`.

