## 18. Troubleshooting

| Symptom | Fix |
|---|---|
| `streamlit: command not found` | Activate the virtual environment, or run `python -m streamlit run app.py`. |
| `ModuleNotFoundError` | Run `pip install -r requirements.txt` inside the activated environment. |
| Port 8501 already in use | `streamlit run app.py --server.port 8502` |
| Browser doesn't open | Copy the `Local URL` from the terminal into your browser. |
| First page of *Score an Order* is slow | The model and SHAP load once in the background; later interactions are fast. |
| Charts look unstyled after a theme change | Restart Streamlit (theme settings in `.streamlit/config.toml` are read at start-up). |
| Garbled characters / `UnicodeEncodeError` on Windows | Set `PYTHONUTF8=1` (PowerShell: `$env:PYTHONUTF8 = "1"`). |
| `FileNotFoundError: DataCoSupplyChainDataset.csv` | Only needed for the full pipeline; download it into `data/raw/` (section 16). The dashboard does not need it. |
| `CutoffError` during step 3 | The stability guard fired: a cutoff moved the flagged share by ≥ 5 points. This is deliberate — inspect the validation score gaps instead of overriding it. |
| Batch upload says "missing required column" | Use the template download on the *Batch Scoring* page; required columns are `Shipping_Mode`, `Type`, `order_value`, `n_items`. |

